      "role": "user",
      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `CharSetTest_testSerialization.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/commons-lang/manual/testcases/CharSetTest/CharSetTest_testSerialization.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write an improved version of the test. The original test has three repetitive `CharSet.getInstance`/`SerializationUtils.clone`/`assertEquals` triplets. I'll refactor into a `@ParameterizedTest` to eliminate the duplication and make the intent (each pattern survives a serialization round-trip) crystal clear.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored test replaces three repetitive clone-and-assert blocks with a single `@ParameterizedTest` driven by `@ValueSource`, making it immediately clear that the same serialization round-trip check applies to a single character, a range, and a mixed/negated expression."
    }
  ],
  "last_code": "package org.apache.commons.lang3;\n\nimport static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;\n\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.DisplayName;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.params.ParameterizedTest;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.params.provider.ValueSource;\n\n/**\n * Verifies that {@link CharSet} is serializable and that equality is preserved\n * after a full serialization/deserialization round-trip.\n */\npublic class CharSetTest_testSerialization extends AbstractLangTest {\n\n    /**\n     * A CharSet created from each pattern must be equal to its deserialized clone,\n     * covering a single character, a character range, and a mixed/negated expression.\n     */\n    @ParameterizedTest(name = \"pattern \\\"{0}\\\" survives serialization round-trip\")\n    @DisplayName(\"CharSet equality is preserved after serialization and deserialization\")\n    @ValueSource(strings = {\n        \"a\",          // single character\n        \"a-e\",        // character range\n        \"be-f^a-z\"    // mixed: literal 'b', range 'e-f', negated range '^a-z'\n    })\n    void testSerialization(final String pattern) {\n        final CharSet original = CharSet.getInstance(pattern);\n        assertEquals(original, SerializationUtils.clone(original));\n    }\n}\n",
